& [PrunedP01] is generic public canonical encoder framework
  + [reason] one closed grammar has no second governed consumer and public generality widens compatibility authority
  + [retained] private profile-specific encoding helpers only

& [PrunedP02] is extraction or widening of the supplied-content accumulator
  + [reason] direct use of already available sha2 avoids coupling two semantically distinct transforms
  + [retained] dependency precedent and streaming proof pattern, not public implementation authority

& [PrunedP03] is whole-inventory canonical byte output
  + [reason] no current consumer requires it and it adds allocation and alternate-authority risks
  + [retained] incremental writes directly into one private hash sink

& [PrunedP04] is canonical decoder, migration, and negotiation
  + [reason] version 0.1 is strict producer-only syntax with no legacy persisted input
  + [retained] exact profile rejection and future new-profile requirement

& [PrunedP05] is Merkle tree and random-access proof structure
  + [reason] TopologyReceipt currently names one aggregate ordered_inventory_sha256 and no partial-proof consumer exists
  + [retained] one sequence-sensitive aggregate SHA-256

& [PrunedP06] is policy and proof-lineage inclusion
  + [reason] receipt schema already separates policy and predecessor bindings from inventory record content
  + [retained] full lineage in the output wrapper beside, not inside, digest bytes

& [PrunedP07] is receipt fragment or consistency-class output
  + [reason] physical root, repeat inventory, time, nonce, policy, predecessor, and issuance authority are absent
  + [retained] supplied_structural_commitment evidence grade only

& [PrunedP08] is physical, Git, database, neural, distributed, and FPGA extension
  + [reason] every such effect or architecture is outside the selected pure dependency seam
  + [retained] no-effect software oracle suitable for later comparison

& [GrowthG01] private hash-sink writer is accepted conditionally
  + [shape] one private helper owns Sha256 and exposes only exact primitive and field-writing methods
  + [constraint] it cannot accept arbitrary tags, field order, serializers, or caller-controlled framing

& [GrowthG02] compile-time tag constants are accepted
  + [shape] private named constants mirror the closed source table
  + [constraint] static tests must detect missing, duplicate within namespace, or changed literal values

& [GrowthG03] independent test-only reference encoder is accepted
  + [shape] test code constructs at least one full expected byte vector separately from production helpers
  + [constraint] it never enters production output or becomes public API

& [GrowthG04] future digest-comparison wrapper is deferred
  + [reason] comparing independently produced inventories has physical and temporal meanings not available here
  + [routing] separately preserve and govern only after two producer results and comparison authority exist

& [GrowthG05] future encoding profile evolution is deferred
